  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `{cite}` of `requirements.cli.mdbook` on `struct[Definition]` (src/lib.rs:121-126) is the right role.\n\n- **Not a test.** The item is a plain data struct, so `{test}` does not apply.\n- **Not an `{impl}`.** `Definition` holds `path`, `text` and `kind`. It makes no decision, performs no check and produces no output. It does not configure `book.toml`, define the `mdbook` subcommand, or render anything.\n- **A `{cite}` fits.** The struct is the in-memory record that `preprocess_book` fills in (src/lib.rs:176-272, which carries the `{impl}` of the requirement). Rendering code in src/index.rs, such as `render_detail_page`, reads it. It exists to carry requirement definitions through the mdBook preprocessor, so a change to what the requirement says about rendering definitions could require changing it.\n- **No redundancy.** The item has no `{impl}` or `{test}` on the same requirement.\n\nI found no gap.",
